      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## How this workflow is wired\n\n**Model path** (the \"brain\" that paints):\n`UNET Loader` -> `Lora Loader` -> `QwenImage21 Cache` -> `KSampler.model`\n\n**Text path** (turns your prompt into numbers the brain understands):\n`CLIP Loader` -> `TextEncodeQwenImage21` -> `KSampler.positive / negative`\n\n**Image path** (turns the brain's internal data into pixels):\n`KSampler` -> `VAE Decode` -> `Save Image`\n\n**Size path**:\n`ResolutionSelector` -> `Empty Latent Image` -> `KSampler.latent_image`\n\n### Things to know\n- LoRA is optional. This workflow HAS it. If you delete the LoRA node,\n  reconnect UNET Loader straight to QwenImage21 Cache, and raise **steps to 25**.\n- **steps must match the LoRA**: 8-step LoRA -> steps = 8. No LoRA -> steps = 25.\n  Mismatch gives blurry / dirty images.\n- `cfg` stays at 1.0 for the official path. `negative_prompt` is ignored at cfg 1.\n- LoRA strength 1.0 is normal. Lower it (0.6) to blend the effect more softly.\n- Changing the prompt is expensive (re-runs the text encoder, ~30s).\n  Changing only the **seed** is cheap. So: fix the prompt, vary the seed.\n- Transparent background: take the 2.1 image-edit template instead of this one.\n"
      ]
    }
